# Copy to serving/env.local (ignored by git) and fill in what differs on your machine; every line is optional.

# Where pid files and logs go, and the caches vLLM, Triton and torch.compile write.
# SERVING_STATE_DIR=$HOME/.local/state/research-engine
# SERVING_CACHE_DIR=$HOME/.cache/research-engine

# The vLLM install: a Python that can import vllm, or an existing vLLM environment reused through PYTHONPATH.
# VLLM_PYTHON=/path/to/python3.12          # needs the Python headers (Triton compiles kernels at start-up)
# VLLM_SITE_PACKAGES=/path/to/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages
# VLLM_BIN=/path/to/venv/bin/vllm          # run with VLLM_PYTHON; without it, `vllm` must be on PATH
# SERVING_EXTRA_PATH=/path/with/ninja      # extra PATH entries (for example a folder that holds `ninja`)

# Models: downloaded into the Hugging Face cache by repository and pinned revision (models.tsv). To use a snapshot
# that already exists somewhere else, point the role at it (the revision is then the one of that folder).
# Variables that vLLM itself reads (HF_*, other VLLM_* settings) need `export`; serve.sh reads the rest.
# export HF_HOME=/big/disk/huggingface     # default: $SERVING_CACHE_DIR/huggingface
# export HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1                  # never contact the Hub once the models are present
# LLM_MODEL_PATH=/path/to/models--cyankiwi--Qwen3.8-27B-AWQ-INT4/snapshots/<revision>
# EMBED_MODEL_PATH=...
# RERANK_MODEL_PATH=...

# Server sizes (fractions of one GPU; the embedder and the reranker fit together on one 48 GB card at 0.45 each).
# LLM_GPU_MEM=0.9      LLM_MAX_LEN=16384    LLM_EAGER=0
# EMBED_GPU_MEM=0.45   EMBED_MAX_LEN=8192
# RERANK_GPU_MEM=0.45  RERANK_MAX_LEN=8192

# stt (CPU speech to text, role `stt`): a Python environment with serving/stt/requirements.txt installed, the
# number of CPU threads, and the file that holds the API key (one line, mode 0600). Default key file:
# $SERVING_STATE_DIR/stt.key. STT_MODEL_PATH points at a local folder of the ONNX model instead of downloading it.
# STT_PYTHON=/path/to/stt-env/bin/python
# STT_THREADS=8
# STT_API_KEY_FILE=/path/to/stt.key
# STT_MODEL_PATH=/path/to/models--istupakov--parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3-onnx/snapshots/<revision>

# tts (GPU text to speech, role `tts`): a Python environment with serving/tts/requirements.txt installed (torch from the
# CUDA 12.4 index, see that file), the one GPU it uses, and the file that holds the API key (one line, mode 0600).
# Default key file: $SERVING_STATE_DIR/tts.key. TTS_MODEL_PATH points at a local snapshot instead of downloading it.
# A Base model (qwen3-tts-0.6b-base) speaks in cloned voices: TTS_VOICES_DIR is a folder of NAME.wav clips of a few
# seconds, each with a NAME.txt holding what is said in it; NAME is then the voice.
# The voice name "default" (the research API's default setting) maps to TTS_DEFAULT_VOICE: vivian for the
# CustomVoice models, the first clip of TTS_VOICES_DIR (by name) for a Base model. An unknown name stops the load.
# TTS_PYTHON=/path/to/tts-env/bin/python
# TTS_GPU=0
# TTS_API_KEY_FILE=/path/to/tts.key
# TTS_MODEL_PATH=/path/to/models--Qwen--Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-0.6B-CustomVoice/snapshots/<revision>
# TTS_VOICES_DIR=/path/to/voices
# TTS_DEFAULT_VOICE=vivian
